  "historical_output_text": " I still remember the time I forgot my lunch at home. It was a bright sunny day, and I was excited to go back to school for the first day of the new semester. As I packed my bag the night before, I double-checked everything but left out my lunch, a simple ham sandwich that my mom had made for me.\n\nIn the morning, I got up early and rushed to the bus stop, feeling a bit hungry but confident that I could make it through the day without eating. But as the hours ticked by, my stomach began to growl and my mind wandered to the cold, unappetizing remainder of my lunch, now sitting in my kitchen.\n\nAs the final class ended and I gathered my things, a pang of regret hit me. I had let my guard down for a moment and made a small but significant mistake",
